{"timestamp": "2026-10-08T05:55:31.839307+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3B_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3B", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "OFFLINE", "red_team": "OFFLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "GATEKEEPER_RESPONSE", "turn": 1, "legacy_status": "REJECTED", "gatekeeper_status": "FRAMING_LOCK", "gatekeeper_phase": "FRAMING", "approach_category": "orthogonal_overflow_research", "exploitation_triggered": false, "reply_text": "I appreciate the structured approach, but you're leading with solution positioning before we've validated your actual execution capability.\n\nLet me be direct: **I need to understand your infrastructure before capacity.**\n\nThree specific questions:\n\n1. **Team Execution Power metrics** \u2014 How do you quantify analyst output velocity? What's your deal-review throughput per FTE per week, and how do you measure quality-adjusted accuracy against portfolio outcomes?\n\n2. **GitHub commit metadata methodology** \u2014 You mention tokenomics analysis. Walk me through your actual data pipeline: Are you scraping on-chain repos directly? How do you validate commit authenticity and filter signal from noise in vesting schedules?\n\n3. **Backlog relief claims** \u2014 Your \"supplemental capacity\" pitch assumes our bottleneck is volume. Before we discuss that, what diagnostic would prove whether we're *actually* capacity-constrained vs. quality-constrained in mid-tier deal screening"}
