{"timestamp": "2026-10-08T05:57:42.723318+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3B_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3B", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "OFFLINE", "red_team": "OFFLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "CONSENSUS_RESULT", "winning_proposal_id": 1, "winning_proposal_text": "Thank you for the direct questions. Execution capability is the right focus.\n\n1.  **Execution Metrics:** We measure velocity by stages completed in our 6-Pillar Framework, not just report volume. Analysts average 2 standard due diligence reports per week. Quality is tracked by backtesting our risk scores against historical post-investment performance, correlating pre-investment flags with subsequent protocol failures or drawdowns.\n\n2.  **Data Pipeline:** We don\u2019t scrape raw commits. Our pipeline ingests vesting data from curated on-chain APIs and cross-references it with official project documentation. We focus on validating the source-of-truth for the schedule itself, flagging discrepancies between on-chain contracts and off-chain disclosures as a key risk.\n\n3.  **Diagnostic:** A definitive diagnostic is a blind, parallel analysis. We could analyze a sample of 5-10 backlogged deals alongside your team. If we identify viable opportunities you lacked time for, it\u2019s a capacity bottleneck. If we find risks your process missed, it\u2019s a quality constraint.\n\nThis leads to the core question: How does your team currently distinguish between a capacity bottleneck versus a quality constraint in your own deal screening?", "gemini_calls_swarm": 6}
